    "reasoning": "The supplied worked solutions confirm every intended MA selection below. No captured grade is supplied. q-40347 has alternating signs at -2, 1/2, and 3, giving (-2,1/2) union (3,infinity). q-90485 has positive signs before -1 and between 1/2 and 5, including endpoints. q-116595 is nonnegative outside [-5,7] and also vanishes at the isolated point -2. q-116614 factors as x^2(x-4)(x+7), giving the two exterior intervals and the isolated zero 0. q-98161 and q-107494 use MA's stated principal-root-of-unity convention k=1 in e^{2\\pi i k/n}. q-162310 requires a unit regular octagon containing 1; q-162241 requires a unit regular pentagon containing 1. q-216710 highlights k=5 among six roots, giving e^{5\\pi i/3}; q-216706 highlights k=3 among seven roots, giving e^{6\\pi i/7}. For the remaining questions, the solutions explicitly interpret the captured fraction-form notation as binomial coefficients. Under that interpretation, q-112325 gives C(3,3)=1, q-69718 gives C(4,2)=6, q-113617 gives C(6,2)=15, and q-113618 gives C(7,5)=21. Pascal's identity supplies C(2,0) for q-69669 and C(2,2) for q-69722. However, these two equations have multiple valid listed expressions: q-69669 options 0, 2, 3, and 4 all equal 1; q-69722 options 0, 1, 3, and 4 all equal 1. Their intended Pascal terms are source-confirmed, but the single-choice questions are mathematically nonunique. This preserves the earlier final ambiguity finding. The fraction-form notation also differs from standard binomial notation; the selections use the interpretation explicitly established by the worked solutions.",
